{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Counters are used to store and display ad-hoc sequences of numbers or Latin characters."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Counters are a poorly defined feature in AsciiDoc and should be avoided if possible. If you do use counters, you should only used them for the most rudimentary use cases, such as making a sequence in a list, table column, or prose. You should "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "not"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "strong",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " use counters to build IDs (i.e., references) or reference text. Using counters across the boundaries of a reference will very likely result in unexpected behavior."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "warning"
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "A counter is implemented as a specialized document attribute. You declare and display a counter using an attribute reference, where the attribute name is prefixed with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "counter:"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " (e.g., "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "{counter:name}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "). Since counters are attributes, counter names follow the same rules as "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "attribute names"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "names-and-values.html#user-defined"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". The most important rule to note is that letters in counter names "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "must be lowercase"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "emphasis",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The counter value is incremented and displayed every time the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "counter:"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " attribute reference is resolved. The term "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "increment"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "strong",
            "roles": [
              "term"
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " means to advance the attribute value to the next value in the sequence. If the counter value is an integer, add 1. If the counter value is a character, move to the next letter in the Latin alphabet (e.g., a → b). The default start value of a counter is 1."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To create a sequence starting at 1, use the simple form "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "{counter:name}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " as shown here:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The salad calls for {counter:seq1}) apples, {counter:seq1}) oranges and {counter:seq1}) pears."
          }
        ],
        "language": "asciidoc",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Here’s the resulting output:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The salad calls for 1) apples, 2) oranges and 3) pears."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "If you want to use a counter value in a section title, you should define it first using an attribute reference."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ":seq1: {counter:seq1}\n== Section {seq1}\n\nThe sequence in this section is {seq1}.\n\n:seq1: {counter:seq1}\n== Section {seq1}\n\nThe sequence in this section is {seq1}."
          }
        ],
        "language": "asciidoc",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Here’s the resulting output:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "floating_title",
            "id": "_section_1",
            "level": 1,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Section 1"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The sequence in this section is 1."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "floating_title",
            "id": "_section_2",
            "level": 1,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Section 2"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The sequence in this section is 2."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To increment the counter without displaying it (i.e., to skip an item in the sequence), use the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "counter2"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " prefix instead:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "{counter2:seq1}"
          }
        ],
        "language": "asciidoc",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "A "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "counter2"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " attribute reference on a line by itself will produce an empty paragraph. You’ll need to adjoin it to the nearest content to avoid this side effect."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "warning"
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To display the current value of the counter without incrementing it, reference the counter name as you would any other attribute:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "{counter2:pnum}This is paragraph {pnum}."
          }
        ],
        "language": "asciidoc",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To create a character sequence, or start a number sequence with a value other than 1, specify a start value by appending it to the first use of the counter:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Dessert calls for {counter:seq1:A}) mangoes, {counter:seq1}) grapes and {counter:seq1}) cherries."
          }
        ],
        "language": "asciidoc",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Character sequences either run from a,b,c,…​x,y,z,{,|…​ or A,B,C,…​,X,Y,Z,[,…​ depending on the start value. Therefore, they aren’t really useful for more than 26 items."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "caution"
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The start value of a counter is only recognized if the counter is "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "unset"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "emphasis",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " at that point in the document. Otherwise, the start value is ignored."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To reset a counter attribute, unset the corresponding attribute using an attribute entry. The attribute entry must be adjacent to a block or else it is ignored."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The salad calls for {counter:seq1:1}) apples, {counter:seq1}) oranges and {counter:seq1}) pears.\n\n:!seq1:\nDessert calls for {counter:seq1:A}) mangoes, {counter:seq1}) grapes and {counter:seq1}) cherries."
          }
        ],
        "language": "asciidoc",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "This gives:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The salad calls for 1) apples, 2) oranges and 3) pears."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Dessert calls for A) mangoes, B) grapes and C) cherries."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Here’s a full example that shows how to use a counter for part numbers in a table."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ".Parts{counter2:index:0}\n|===\n|Part Id |Description\n\n|PX-{counter:index}\n|Description of PX-{index}\n\n|PX-{counter:index}\n|Description of PX-{index}\n|==="
          }
        ],
        "language": "asciidoc",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Here’s the output of that table:"
          }
